sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant Agent as DevOps Agent
    participant APIGW as API Gateway<br/>(SigV4 Auth)
    participant Server as MCP Server<br/>(Lambda)
    participant CB as Circuit Breaker
    participant Policy as Policy Engine
    participant Jira as Jira Cloud
    participant Audit as CloudWatch<br/>Audit Log

    Note over Agent, Jira: POLICY DENIED PATH — Agent tries a forbidden action

    Agent->>+APIGW: POST /prod/mcp<br/>{"method":"tools/call","params":{"name":"update_issue",<br/>"arguments":{"issue_key":"KAN-1","fields":{"security_level":"Internal"}}}}
    APIGW->>+Server: Invoke Lambda

    Server->>CB: is_open()?
    CB-->>Server: false

    %% Policy check FAILS
    Server->>+Policy: check_field_writes("KAN", {"security_level": "Internal"})
    Policy->>Policy: Load policy.yaml
    Policy->>Policy: "security_level" ∈ forbidden_fields?
    Note right of Policy: YES — field is<br/>explicitly forbidden<br/>for project KAN
    Policy-->>-Server: THROW PolicyDenied<br/>("field 'security_level' is forbidden in project KAN")

    Note over Server, Jira: Jira is NEVER called.<br/>Denial happens before<br/>any external request.

    %% Audit the denial
    Server->>Audit: [AUDIT] {"event":"policy_denied",<br/>"tool":"update_issue",<br/>"reason":"field 'security_level' is forbidden in project KAN"}

    Server-->>-APIGW: {"jsonrpc":"2.0","result":{"content":[{<br/>"type":"text",<br/>"text":"{\"error\":\"POLICY_DENIED\",\"message\":\"...\"}"<br/>}]}}
    APIGW-->>-Agent: 200 OK

    Note over Agent: Agent receives structured error.<br/>Reports denial to user gracefully.<br/>No retry needed — this is a hard policy constraint.
